{"step":"3-blockscan-p4","measured":"bulk IN bytes after writing one byte value at one address of a register space the byte scans had not covered, on top of the baseline","harness":{"crates_rtl_head":"387a74c","harness_uncommitted":true},"unix_time":1791428487,"bench":"RTL2832U + R820T-family tuner, 28.8 MHz crystal, behind a USB analyzer with switchable TARGET-A power; no signal source, antenna input sees noise only","k":"header","block":"p4","candidate_space":"demodulator page 4 (request block 0, wIndex page 4), wValue = offset << 8 | 0x20 (step 1C): offset 0x00..=0xFF (wValue 0x0000..=0x00FF) x value 0x00..=0xFF, except the value the address holds when its candidate comes up (logged as kind s); iterated offset, value in ascending order with no reordering; 65536 candidates","bound":"Table 27 (p. 36) gives the demodulator pages 0-4 and documents no register on page 4. Offsets 0x00-0xFF, the whole page, as for pages 0-2","byte_addressing":"USB and system registers are 32-bit little-endian words (step 1A, data/step1-sys-usb-encoding.json; step 1D, data/step1-writes.json); byte reads inside them work (step 1A); each candidate is one byte written with wLength 1 at one address, and whether the chip takes a one-byte write into a 32-bit register is what the read-back (in / rb) records; demodulator pages are byte registers","already_known":"bit scan (data/step3-scan.jsonl, 2048 candidates on page 4): 0 bytes; writes at 0x08 (bits 0-7 cleared AD_EN: baseline disturbed), 0x10 (bit 1: a demodulator soft reset, baseline disturbed, restore stalled), 0x20 (bit 4) and 0xA7 (bits 5, 6) wedged the chip - the same offsets and effects as page 0's, so page 4 writes reach page 0's registers there; at bit 0 page 4's reads equalled page 0's at 106 of 256 offsets, and page 4 read 0x00 everywhere but 0x00 (0x04), 0x01 (0x02), 0x1C (0x03), 0x46 (0x10), 0x56 (0x20), 0xAD (0x0A). Every offset is covered regardless","hazards":"the bit scan's: 0x08 clears AD_EN, 0x10 bit 1 resets the demodulator, 0x20 bit 4 and 0xA7 bits 5-6 wedge the chip (power cycle)","method":"plain, as data/step3-bytescan.jsonl: the value is written into the running chip with no restart between candidates (METHODS.md section 5: every declared space covered once before any is repeated with a variant)","settings_held_fixed":"documented-only baseline at 2400000 Hz; 4 x 16384 byte bulk transfers queued; window 50 ms right after the read-back, then a 200 ms follow-up window if any byte arrived, then a 50 ms window after the restore","window_justification":"the plain byte scan's (data/step3-bytescan.jsonl header): 4.8 MB/s fills a 16 KiB transfer every 3.4 ms, so 50 ms expects ~14.6 transfers (one-transfer quantisation 6.8 % < 20 % tolerance); any byte triggers the 200 ms follow-up, so a stream that starts up to ~50 ms after the write is still judged","streams_criterion":"within 20% of 2 x 2400000 bytes/s in the window or the follow-up","line_legend":"k: c candidate / s skip (the address's current value) / setup / recovery; o offset in the block (decimal); v value; orig the byte read before the write (null = the read failed); in the read-back after the write equals v; rb the read-back when it differs (absent when in); d bytes completed between candidates, discarded before the write (absent when 0); b bytes from the write to the end of the last window (window + follow-up); bps the follow-up window's bytes/s (absent without bytes); s streams; q the bulk detector's self-check from the previous candidate's last window to the end of the window, qf the same for the follow-up, qa for the after-restore window: [transfers submitted, completed, completed with an error, halts (Stall completions, each cleared by ClearFeature ENDPOINT_HALT), fewest transfers in flight, endpoint halted at any point 0/1]; e errors and events (absent when none); w wedged -> power cycle and re-baseline (next line k=recovery)","procedure":"read the byte (skip if equal); discard completed transfers; write the value; read it back; window; on bytes the follow-up; restore the original and verify by read-back; on bytes the after-restore window; chip answering?; baseline re-checked (DEMOD_CTL, AD_EN, en_bbin, rsamp_ratio, USB_SYSCTL DMA, USB_EPA_CFG, USB_EPA_CTL, USB_EPA_MAXPKT): reapplied if disturbed, power cycle if it does not hold; a chip that stops answering or keeps streaming after the restore is power-cycled and re-baselined; the scan does not stop on a hit"}
{"power_cycle":{"devices_before":1,"vbus_off_reply":"TARGET A vbus off (discharging)","disappeared_after_ms":62,"off_time_ms":500,"vbus_on_reply":"TARGET A vbus on","reappeared_after_ms":503,"devices_after_settle":1},"baseline_writes":[{"write":"DEMOD_CTL |= PLL|ADC_I|ADC_Q|reset-release (Table 15)","result":{"before":"0x20","after":"0xE8"},"item":"DemodCtl"},{"write":"GPIO3: GPD[3]=0 output, GPOE[3]=1, GPO[3]=0 power on (Tables 16-19)","result":{"GPD":{"before":"0x06","after":"0x06"},"GPOE":{"before":"0x19","after":"0x19"},"GPO":{"before":"0x18","after":"0x10"}},"item":"TunerPower"},{"write":"page 0 0x08[7:6] = 11 AD_EN_reg, AD_EN_reg1 (Table 4, zero-IF §9.1)","result":{"before":"0x0D","after":"0xCD","verified":true},"item":"AdEn"},{"write":"page 1 0xB1[0] = 1 en_bbin (Table 4, zero-IF §9.1)","result":{"before":"0x1F","after":"0x1F","verified":true},"item":"EnBbin"},{"write":"pset_iffreq = 0 (Table 6, §9.3 zero IF)","result":[{"before":"0x35","after":"0x00","verified":true},{"before":"0xD7","after":"0x00","verified":true},{"before":"0x5D","after":"0x00","verified":true}],"item":"IfFreqZero"},{"write":"rsamp_ratio = 0x3000000 for 2400000 Hz (Table 7, §9.4)","result":[{"before":"0xF3","after":"0xFC","verified":true},{"before":"0x26","after":"0x00","verified":true},{"before":"0x66","after":"0x00","verified":true},{"before":"0x64","after":"0x00","verified":true}],"item":"Rsamp"},{"write":"USB_EPA_MAXPKT = descriptor wMaxPacketSize (Table 33)","result":{"before":"0x00000200","after":"0x00000200"},"item":"EpaMaxPkt"},{"write":"USB_EPA_CFG: enable, type bulk, number from the descriptor (Table 31)","result":{"before":"0x000000D1","after":"0x000000D1"},"item":"EpaCfg"},{"write":"USB_EPA_CTL: FIFO reset 1 then 0, stall 0 (Table 32)","result":[{"before":"0x00000000","after":"0x00000200"},{"before":"0x00000200","after":"0x00000000"}],"item":"EpaFifoReset"},{"write":"USB_SYSCTL[0] = 1 DMA enable (Table 30)","result":{"before":"0x00000001","after":"0x00000001"},"item":"Dma"}],"k":"setup","detector":"4 bulk IN transfers of 16384 bytes kept in flight: every completion resubmitted at once, topped up before each wait; a Stall completion = endpoint halted -> queued transfers cancelled, ClearFeature(ENDPOINT_HALT) sent (USB 2.0 9.4.1, 9.4.5), its result recorded, queue refilled; every error completion counted by kind. Line fields q / qf / qa = [submitted, completed, errored, halts, fewest in flight, halted at any point 0/1]"}
